LAST_SUCCESS=Task 36 step 6 — Kotlin/Wasm smoke consumer wart-app-md-smoke/ built end-to-end on dev box. Hand-written WIT bindings (MarkdownImports.kt) since wit-bindgen 0.53.1 has no Kotlin generator (skiko's header is misleading; that tool is private). Build pipeline lands cleanly: (1) gradle compileProductionExecutableKotlinWasmWasi → 94 KB Kotlin wasm; (2) wasm-tools component embed --world md-smoke wit/ + deps/markdown/ → embedded; (3) wasm-tools component new --adapt wasi_snapshot_preview1.command.wasm → 113 KB component declaring `import war:markdown/renderer@0.1.0` + `export wasi:cli/run@0.2.6`; (4) wac plug --plug markdown_renderer.wasm → 454 KB composed component. Built command-variant adapter alongside reactor (wasmtime-src/target/.../wasi_snapshot_preview1.command.wasm) so the command-adapter pathway is available. Canonical-ABI caveat caught: render's IMPORT side is `[i32 i32 i32] -> []` (caller-allocated return area), asymmetric from the EXPORT side (callee-allocated, `[i32 i32] -> [i32]`) — fixed by updating @WasmImport + allocating an 8-byte return area in render().
NOTES=Open issue (not blocking step 7): empty main() runs+exits clean; any meaningful body (println or render call) trips "thrown Wasm exception" at runtime under wasmtime CLI. Structurally proven the wiring (composed component validates, exports/imports match); diagnosing the Kotlin/Wasm + command-adapter println interaction is a follow-up. Step 7 next: device-verify through wart-host (which sets up wasi stdio differently — wart-host's wasi_stderr.rs routes fd 2 to logcat, different from `wasmtime run`'s pipe-to-tty path). Plan: install markdown system bundle on device, install the smoke consumer as an app, run via a new wart-host mode that drives `wasi:cli/run` (vs current standalone path which expects skiko-ui). If wart-host's stdio routing makes println work, full end-to-end smoke; otherwise observe via exit code + the loader's log lines proving "loaded installed:..." + "dep markdown instantiated".
